              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گروه کر (goruh-e kor) — \"a choir\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دخترم در گروه کر مدرسه آواز میخواند. dokhtaram dar goruh-e kor-e madrese âvâz mikhânad. My daughter sings in the school choir."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "goruh 'group' + kor 'choir'. Not kar 'deaf', spelled the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "goruh-e kor joins inherited goruh, 'group', which EtymDB traces to a Middle Persian word for 'group, crowd' (EtymDB), and kor, a modern loan usually traced to French chœur, 'choir'. EtymDB's entry for this spelling is the other word, kar, 'deaf'."
            }
          ]
        },
